Third-party code and attribution
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. CorrCLIP -- https://github.com/zdk258/CorrCLIP
   Pinned commit: 6c1fd2c02ff90f071ed744a5998be0cda7ad75b4

   GramSeg's evaluation harness is CorrCLIP's. The upstream repository ships
   NO top-level LICENSE file, which means its source is "all rights reserved"
   and CANNOT be redistributed here.

   Consequently this repository contains NO CorrCLIP source code. Our changes
   to it are distributed as minimal unified diffs under patches/, which the
   user applies to their own upstream checkout. See patches/README.md.

2. Trident -- https://github.com/YuHengsss/Trident
   Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

   The interchangeability experiment ("slot-in" study) drops our Gram affinity
   kernel into Trident's correlation slot. Any Trident-derived code the user
   assembles by following our instructions remains under Trident's Apache-2.0
   terms; attribution to the Trident authors is required.

3. SED -- https://github.com/xb534/SED
   Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

   legacy/sed_frozen/ contains our own adapter / frozen-training scripts from
   an abandoned exploration that targeted SED as its base. They import SED and
   detectron2 APIs but contain no verbatim SED source.

4. Upstream models and libraries used at runtime (not redistributed here):
   - DINOv3 / DINOv2 (Meta AI) -- frozen ViT backbones, subject to Meta's
     respective model licenses; obtain weights from the official source.
   - dino.txt (Meta AI) -- text head used only as a comparison baseline.
   - OpenCLIP / MetaCLIP -- CLIP weights and tokenizer.
   - SAM 2 (Meta AI) -- used only as a baseline mask source for comparison.
   - Stable Diffusion 2.1-base -- used only to run a diffusion-based baseline.
   - MMSegmentation / MMEngine (OpenMMLab) -- Apache-2.0, evaluation protocol.

   Each of the above is governed by its own license. Users are responsible for
   obtaining these weights and complying with their terms.
